{"title":"Clinical Physiotherapist Roadmap","role":"Clinical Physiotherapist","summary":"A Clinical Physiotherapist evaluates movement and functional limitations and provides rehabilitation interventions to improve mobility, strength, balance, coordination, pain management, and independence. With exposure to sports, neurological, and paediatric rehabilitation, the professional can work across multiple patient populations.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Physiotherapy - Sports / Neuro / Paediatric Rehabilitation"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Clinical Physiotherapist evaluates movement and functional limitations and provides rehabilitation interventions to improve mobility, strength, balance, coordination, pain management, and independence. With exposure to sports, neurological, and paediatric rehabilitation, the professional can work across multiple patient populations."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical workplaces include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Physiotherapy and rehabilitation clinics"},{"text":"Sports medicine centres"},{"text":"Orthopaedic centres"},{"text":"Neurological rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Paediatric rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Multidisciplinary rehabilitation hospitals"},{"text":"Fitness and sports-performance facilities"},{"text":"Home healthcare services"},{"text":"Research and academic institutions"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Clinical practice, professional title, registration, and permitted scope depend on the recognized qualification, applicable registration requirements, institution, and current regulations."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Possible Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry Level"},{"text":"Clinical Physiotherapist, Junior Physiotherapist"}],[{"text":"1–3 Years"},{"text":"Physiotherapist, Rehabilitation Therapist"}],[{"text":"3–6 Years"},{"text":"Senior Physiotherapist, Specialist Physiotherapist"}],[{"text":"5–10 Years"},{"text":"Physiotherapy Unit Coordinator, Clinical Supervisor"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Sports Physiotherapist, Neuro Physiotherapist, Paediatric Physiotherapist"}],[{"text":"Management"},{"text":"Rehabilitation Centre Manager, Clinical Operations Coordinator"}],[{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Clinical Research Assistant, Rehabilitation Researcher"}],[{"text":"Academic"},{"text":"Physiotherapy Educator / Lecturer after appropriate higher qualification"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Physiotherapy Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Human physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Basic pathology"},{"text":"Exercise science"},{"text":"Kinesiology"},{"text":"Biomechanics"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Basic patient care"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Pay special attention to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Musculoskeletal anatomy"},{"text":"Peripheral nerves"},{"text":"Brain and spinal cord"},{"text":"Gait mechanics"},{"text":"Joint movement"},{"text":"Muscle actions"},{"text":"Paediatric development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Assessment & Treatment Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop competency in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient history taking"},{"text":"Physical examination"},{"text":"Range-of-motion assessment"},{"text":"Muscle strength testing"},{"text":"Postural assessment"},{"text":"Gait assessment"},{"text":"Balance assessment"},{"text":"Pain assessment"},{"text":"Functional assessment"},{"text":"Exercise prescription"},{"text":"Therapeutic exercises"},{"text":"Basic electrotherapy"},{"text":"Manual therapy fundamentals"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to document:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient History","Physical Examination","Functional Assessment","Clinical Findings","Physiotherapy Assessment","Treatment Planning","Intervention","Reassessment","Progress Documentation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3/4 — Clinical Specialization"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop practical exposure to three major areas."},{"type":"h","text":"Sports Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn about:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sports injuries"},{"text":"Muscle strains"},{"text":"Ligament injuries"},{"text":"Tendinopathies"},{"text":"Joint injuries"},{"text":"Return-to-sport planning"},{"text":"Functional movement"},{"text":"Strength and conditioning"},{"text":"Injury prevention"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neurological Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stroke rehabilitation"},{"text":"Spinal cord injuries"},{"text":"Traumatic brain injury"},{"text":"Parkinsonian disorders"},{"text":"Multiple sclerosis"},{"text":"Cerebral palsy"},{"text":"Peripheral nerve disorders"},{"text":"Balance and gait dysfunction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Paediatric Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developmental milestones"},{"text":"Cerebral palsy"},{"text":"Developmental delay"},{"text":"Paediatric neurological conditions"},{"text":"Musculoskeletal conditions"},{"text":"Gross motor development"},{"text":"Balance and coordination"},{"text":"Family-centred rehabilitation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core Clinical Skills"},{"type":"table","header":["Skill Area","What to Learn"],"rows":[[{"text":"Assessment"},{"text":"History, physical and functional assessment"}],[{"text":"Musculoskeletal"},{"text":"ROM, strength, posture and movement assessment"}],[{"text":"Neurological"},{"text":"Tone, reflexes, balance and gait assessment"}],[{"text":"Paediatric"},{"text":"Developmental and functional assessment"}],[{"text":"Exercise Therapy"},{"text":"Strength, flexibility, endurance and motor control"}],[{"text":"Manual Therapy"},{"text":"Evidence-based manual techniques"}],[{"text":"Gait Training"},{"text":"Normal and pathological gait"}],[{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Static and dynamic balance training"}],[{"text":"Pain Management"},{"text":"Non-pharmacological rehabilitation strategies"}],[{"text":"Electrotherapy"},{"text":"Appropriate modality selection and safe use"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"SOAP notes and treatment records"}],[{"text":"Patient Education"},{"text":"Home exercise and self-management"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Assessment Framework"},{"type":"p","text":"A good physiotherapist should avoid jumping directly to treatment."},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient History","Chief Complaint","Medical / Surgical History","Observation","Palpation","ROM Assessment","Strength Assessment","Neurological / Functional Tests","Movement & Gait Analysis","Clinical Assessment","Treatment Goals","Intervention","Outcome Measurement"]},{"type":"h","text":"Sports Physiotherapy Track"},{"type":"h","text":"Key Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop expertise in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sports injury mechanisms"},{"text":"Acute injury management"},{"text":"Rehabilitation progression"},{"text":"Strength and conditioning"},{"text":"Flexibility"},{"text":"Proprioception"},{"text":"Agility"},{"text":"Plyometrics"},{"text":"Return-to-play testing"},{"text":"Injury prevention"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rehabilitation Model"},{"type":"flow","items":["Injury","Initial Assessment","Pain / Swelling Management","Mobility Restoration","Strength Restoration","Neuromuscular Training","Sport-Specific Training","Functional Testing","Return to Sport"]},{"type":"p","text":"The final return-to-sport decision should follow appropriate clinical assessment and multidisciplinary/team protocols."},{"type":"h","text":"Neuro Physiotherapy Track"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motor control"},{"text":"Muscle tone"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Coordination"},{"text":"Gait"},{"text":"Functional mobility"},{"text":"Postural control"},{"text":"Task-specific training"},{"text":"Neuroplasticity principles"},{"text":"Assistive devices"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neurorehabilitation Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Neurological Assessment","Motor / Sensory Assessment","Tone & Balance Assessment","Functional Assessment","Goal Setting","Task-Specific Training","Gait / Mobility Training","Home Exercise Program","Outcome Measurement"]},{"type":"h","text":"Paediatric Physiotherapy Track"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop skills in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developmental assessment"},{"text":"Gross motor development"},{"text":"Fine motor coordination awareness"},{"text":"Postural control"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Gait"},{"text":"Strength and flexibility"},{"text":"Play-based therapy"},{"text":"Family education"},{"text":"Assistive equipment awareness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Paediatric Approach"},{"type":"flow","items":["Child Assessment","Developmental Profile","Functional Limitations","Family / Caregiver Input","Individual Goals","Play-Based Intervention","Functional Training","Home Program","Progress Review"]},{"type":"p","text":"The child's age, developmental stage, communication ability, family environment, and functional goals should all be considered."},{"type":"h","text":"Exercise Therapy"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong competency in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Strength"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Isometric exercise"},{"text":"Isotonic exercise"},{"text":"Progressive resistance training"},{"text":"Functional strengthening"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mobility"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Active ROM"},{"text":"Passive ROM"},{"text":"Dynamic mobility"},{"text":"Flexibility training"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Neuromuscular"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Proprioception"},{"text":"Coordination"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Motor control"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cardiopulmonary"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Aerobic conditioning"},{"text":"Breathing exercises"},{"text":"Functional endurance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Plyometrics"},{"text":"Agility"},{"text":"Sport-specific conditioning"},{"text":"Functional movement training"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Manual Therapy"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop foundational knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Soft-tissue techniques"},{"text":"Joint mobilization principles"},{"text":"Muscle energy techniques"},{"text":"Myofascial techniques"},{"text":"Stretching techniques"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Manual therapy should be used as part of a broader evidence-based rehabilitation program rather than as a substitute for active rehabilitation when active treatment is appropriate."},{"type":"h","text":"Electrotherapy & Modalities"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the principles, indications, contraindications, and safe operation of commonly used modalities such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"TENS"},{"text":"NMES"},{"text":"Therapeutic ultrasound"},{"text":"Interferential therapy"},{"text":"Short-wave diathermy"},{"text":"Superficial heat"},{"text":"Cryotherapy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong physiotherapist should understand when a modality is appropriate and when exercise or functional rehabilitation is more important."},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to maintain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient assessment records"},{"text":"Treatment plans"},{"text":"SOAP notes"},{"text":"Progress notes"},{"text":"Outcome measurements"},{"text":"Exercise prescriptions"},{"text":"Home-program records"},{"text":"Discharge summaries"}]},{"type":"h","text":"SOAP Structure"},{"type":"flow","items":["S — Subjective","Patient-reported symptoms and concerns"]},{"type":"flow","items":["O — Objective","Measured clinical findings"]},{"type":"flow","items":["A — Assessment","Clinical interpretation"]},{"type":"flow","items":["P — Plan","Treatment and follow-up plan"]},{"type":"h","text":"Outcome Measurement"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to use appropriate validated outcome measures for different populations."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples include assessment of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pain"},{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Walking ability"},{"text":"Functional independence"},{"text":"Quality of movement"},{"text":"Sports performance"},{"text":"Developmental function"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Using measurable outcomes helps demonstrate whether treatment is actually improving function."},{"type":"h","text":"Technology & Digital Physiotherapy"},{"type":"p","text":"Modern physiotherapy increasingly uses:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Electronic medical records"},{"text":"Tele-rehabilitation"},{"text":"Wearable sensors"},{"text":"Motion tracking"},{"text":"Video gait analysis"},{"text":"Force platforms"},{"text":"Digital exercise platforms"},{"text":"Remote patient monitoring"},{"text":"AI-assisted movement analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful technical skills:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Data visualization"},{"text":"Digital documentation"},{"text":"Basic research methodology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI & Future Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"A future-ready physiotherapist can understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-based movement analysis"},{"text":"Computer vision"},{"text":"Automated gait analysis"},{"text":"Wearable rehabilitation sensors"},{"text":"Robotic rehabilitation"},{"text":"Virtual reality rehabilitation"},{"text":"Augmented reality training"},{"text":"Remote rehabilitation monitoring"},{"text":"Personalized exercise programs"},{"text":"Digital biomarkers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example Future Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Movement Data","Wearable / Camera / Sensor","Digital Analysis","Movement Pattern Identification","Physiotherapist Review","Personalized Rehabilitation","Progress Monitoring"]},{"type":"p","text":"AI should support clinical decision-making rather than replace professional assessment and clinical judgment."},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Project Ideas"},{"type":"h","text":"Sports"},{"type":"h","text":"Analysis of Functional Recovery Following a Structured Sports Rehabilitation Program"},{"type":"h","text":"Neurology"},{"type":"h","text":"Effect of Task-Specific Training on Functional Mobility in Neurological Rehabilitation"},{"type":"h","text":"Paediatrics"},{"type":"h","text":"Assessment of Functional Motor Development in Children Undergoing Physiotherapy"},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"Computer-Vision-Based Gait Analysis for Physiotherapy Assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Wearables"},{"type":"h","text":"Use of Wearable Sensors for Monitoring Rehabilitation Exercises"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Health"},{"type":"h","text":"Development of a Digital Home Exercise and Progress Tracking System"}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Prioritize clinical exposure in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Multispecialty hospitals"},{"text":"Orthopaedic hospitals"},{"text":"Sports medicine centres"},{"text":"Neurological rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Paediatric rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Physiotherapy clinics"},{"text":"Rehabilitation hospitals"},{"text":"Sports academies"},{"text":"Community rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Home healthcare organizations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Try to experience multiple patient populations rather than spending the entire internship in only one setting."}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical Physiotherapist"},{"text":"Junior Physiotherapist"},{"text":"Rehabilitation Physiotherapist"},{"text":"Sports Rehabilitation Assistant"},{"text":"Neurorehabilitation Physiotherapist"},{"text":"Paediatric Physiotherapy Assistant"},{"text":"Hospital Physiotherapist"},{"text":"Outpatient Physiotherapist"},{"text":"Home Rehabilitation Physiotherapist"},{"text":"Rehabilitation Centre Physiotherapist"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Actual eligibility depends on the recognized qualification and applicable professional requirements."},{"type":"h","text":"Employer Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Employer","Most Valuable Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Hospital"},{"text":"Assessment + therapeutic exercise"}],[{"text":"Orthopaedic Centre"},{"text":"Musculoskeletal rehabilitation"}],[{"text":"Sports Centre"},{"text":"Sports injury rehabilitation"}],[{"text":"Neuro Centre"},{"text":"Neuro assessment + gait training"}],[{"text":"Paediatric Centre"},{"text":"Developmental rehabilitation"}],[{"text":"Rehabilitation Hospital"},{"text":"Multidisciplinary rehabilitation"}],[{"text":"Sports Academy"},{"text":"Performance + injury prevention"}],[{"text":"Home Healthcare"},{"text":"Functional rehabilitation + communication"}],[{"text":"Digital Health Company"},{"text":"Clinical knowledge + technology"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Additional Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic Life Support"},{"text":"Sports rehabilitation"},{"text":"Strength and conditioning"},{"text":"Manual therapy"},{"text":"Neurorehabilitation"},{"text":"Paediatric rehabilitation"},{"text":"Taping techniques"},{"text":"Gait analysis"},{"text":"Exercise prescription"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Healthcare quality"},{"text":"Digital health"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Choose certifications based on recognized training providers, practical value, and relevance to the intended specialization."},{"type":"h","text":"Higher Education Options"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on eligibility and institutional offerings:"},{"type":"h","text":"Master's"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MPT Orthopaedics"},{"text":"MPT Neurology"},{"text":"MPT Sports"},{"text":"MPT Paediatrics"},{"text":"MPT Cardiopulmonary"},{"text":"MPT Community Physiotherapy"},{"text":"MPT Rehabilitation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other PG Pathways"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc. Exercise Science"},{"text":"Sports Science"},{"text":"Rehabilitation Science"},{"text":"Healthcare Management"},{"text":"Hospital Administration"},{"text":"Public Health"},{"text":"Clinical Research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"}]},{"heading":"Sports Physiotherapy","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Athletes"},{"text":"Sports injuries"},{"text":"Performance"},{"text":"Injury prevention"},{"text":"Return-to-sport rehabilitation"}]}]},{"heading":"Neuro Physiotherapy","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stroke"},{"text":"Parkinson's disease"},{"text":"Cerebral palsy"},{"text":"Spinal cord injury"},{"text":"Brain injury"},{"text":"Neuromuscular rehabilitation"}]}]},{"heading":"Paediatric Physiotherapy","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developmental delay"},{"text":"Cerebral palsy"},{"text":"Paediatric neurological disorders"},{"text":"Developmental movement"},{"text":"Functional independence"}]}]},{"heading":"Orthopaedic Physiotherapy","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Joint injuries"},{"text":"Post-operative rehabilitation"},{"text":"Spine conditions"},{"text":"Musculoskeletal disorders"}]}]},{"heading":"Geriatric Rehabilitation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Falls prevention"},{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Strength"},{"text":"Functional independence"}]}]},{"heading":"Digital Rehabilitation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tele-rehabilitation"},{"text":"Wearable sensors"},{"text":"AI movement analysis"},{"text":"Digital exercise platforms"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Clinical Physiotherapist","Experienced Physiotherapist","Senior Physiotherapist","Specialist Physiotherapist","Clinical Supervisor","Physiotherapy Department Coordinator","Rehabilitation Manager","Clinical / Rehabilitation Operations Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist Route"},{"type":"flow","items":["Clinical Physiotherapist","MPT / Specialized Training","Specialist Physiotherapist","Advanced Clinical Practice","Clinical Specialist / Consultant-Level Role"]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"p","text":"The future physiotherapy ecosystem is increasingly moving toward:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted movement analysis"},{"text":"Computer vision"},{"text":"Wearable rehabilitation sensors"},{"text":"Robotic rehabilitation"},{"text":"Exoskeleton-assisted rehabilitation"},{"text":"Virtual reality"},{"text":"Tele-rehabilitation"},{"text":"Digital therapeutics"},{"text":"Remote patient monitoring"},{"text":"Personalized rehabilitation"},{"text":"Data-driven clinical decision support"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"p","text":"Anatomy & Physiology"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Kinesiology & Biomechanics"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Clinical Assessment"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Therapeutic Exercise"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Manual Therapy"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Sports Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Neurorehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Paediatric Rehabilitation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Gait & Movement Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Patient Education"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Clinical Documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Evidence-Based Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Digital Health"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"AI / Wearable Technology Awareness"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally be able to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Conduct structured patient assessments"},{"text":"Understand musculoskeletal, neurological, and paediatric conditions"},{"text":"Perform appropriate functional assessments"},{"text":"Design supervised, individualized rehabilitation programs"},{"text":"Apply therapeutic exercise principles"},{"text":"Understand appropriate use of physiotherapy modalities"},{"text":"Perform basic gait and movement analysis"},{"text":"Develop home exercise programs"},{"text":"Track measurable clinical outcomes"},{"text":"Maintain professional clinical documentation"},{"text":"Communicate effectively with patients and caregivers"},{"text":"Work within multidisciplinary healthcare teams"},{"text":"Understand sports injury rehabilitation"},{"text":"Understand neurological rehabilitation"},{"text":"Understand paediatric rehabilitation"},{"text":"Use digital tools for clinical documentation and rehabilitation monitoring"},{"text":"Apply evidence-based reasoning to physiotherapy practice"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"“Clinical Physiotherapist with strong Sports + Neuro + Paediatric Rehabilitation exposure, evidence-based exercise therapy, functional assessment, and digital rehabilitation skills.”"},{"type":"p","text":"This positioning provides a broad clinical foundation while allowing later specialization in sports physiotherapy, neurological rehabilitation, paediatric physiotherapy, orthopaedics, rehabilitation science, or technology-enabled physiotherapy."}]}]}